Package: rekordbox-wine
Architecture: amd64
# The package carries its own Wine at /usr/lib/rekordbox-wine/wine, so no wine
# package is required. These are the system libraries that runtime links or
# dlopen()s for the capabilities rekordbox uses; bin/rbw-runtime-check verifies
# them on every launch.
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 libgnutls30t64 | libgnutls30, libgl1, libegl1, libx11-6, libxext6, libxi6,
 libxrandr2, libxrender1, libxcursor1, libxcomposite1, libxinerama1, libxfixes3,
 libxxf86vm1, libxkbcommon0, libwayland-client0, libfreetype6, libfontconfig1,
 libdbus-1-3, libasound2t64 | libasound2, libusb-1.0-0, libudev1,
 alsa-utils, python3
Recommends: rtkit
Suggests: pipewire-alsa
Description: rekordbox 7.2.x with a DDJ-400 on Linux, on its own patched Wine
 A pinned Wine (11.18 with the wine-staging patchset) with the fixes rekordbox
 needs compiled in, and a launcher that verifies every one of them before
 starting rekordbox. This package does NOT contain rekordbox itself, which is
 proprietary and must be downloaded from rekordbox.com.
 .
 Ten Wine defects are fixed, without which the application paints a single frame
 and freezes, has no working audio device, cannot open its File menu, cannot see
 a USB stick, and rejects the controller it has just detected.
 .
 The Wine lives in /usr/lib/rekordbox-wine/wine. The distribution's Wine is
 neither used nor modified, so a Wine upgrade cannot break rekordbox.
